issue.body:
**Kibana version**: `Kibana 4.5.0` ( kibana-4.5.0-darwin-x64)

**OS version**: Any

**Original install method (e.g. download page, yum, from source, etc.)**: Download page

**Description of the problem including expected versus actual behavior**:

If there is an empty root field, with some fields inside it, a dot is added to the full name of the field, and Kibana thinks that the field isn't mapped, while it is added to the settings.

**Steps to reproduce**:

**[1]**

Configure the index and add some documents:

```
PUT kibana_bug
{
  "mappings": {
    "client-log": {
      "properties": {
        "": {
          "properties": {
            "metric-root-used_percentage": {
              "type": "float"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

GET kibana_bug/_mapping/*/field/.metric-root-used_percentage

POST kibana_bug/client-log
{
  "": {
    "metric-root-used_percentage": 2131
  }
}
```

**[2]**

Configure the index pattern

![screen shot 2016-07-04 at 09 00 38](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1675411/16559800/d569b5f8-41c5-11e6-9400-3ff91f8d1e2c.png)

**[3]**

Verify that:

a) A field with a dot is added

![screen shot 2016-07-04 at 09 01 20](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1675411/16559823/f2057f8a-41c5-11e6-8ae2-429a625820fb.png)

b) The field is not recognized 

![screen shot 2016-07-04 at 09 02 00](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1675411/16559859/2acfc974-41c6-11e6-96a0-4df82de1dd8a.png)

I thinks that it's related to the fact that elasticsearch internally creates a field with a dot with it. If you only get this field by the mapping GET api, you get:

```
{
  "kibana_bug": {
    "mappings": {
      "client-log": {
        ".metric-root-used_percentage": {
          "full_name": ".metric-root-used_percentage",
          "mapping": {
            "metric-root-used_percentage": {
              "type": "float"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
